set-jump: post_election

@1936
on-arrival: {!
Q.industrial = 26;
Q.landless = 25;
Q.smallholder = 20;
Q.urban_middle = 14;
Q.unemployed = 14;
Q.catholic = 30;

Q.classes = ['industrial', 'landless', 'smallholder', 'urban_middle', 'unemployed', 'catholic'];
Q.parties = ['psoe', 'pce', 'ceda', 'izq_rep', 'radical', 'monarchist', 'falange', 'other'];

// The 1936 Popular Front: PSOE + PCE + Republican Left reunited on a joint list.
// The right ran comparatively divided (the Radical Party had collapsed after
// the Straperlo scandal; CEDA and the Monarchists did not fully coalesce).
Q.psoe_in_bloc = 1;
Q.pce_in_bloc = 1;
Q.ceda_in_bloc = 0;
Q.izq_rep_in_bloc = 1;
Q.radical_in_bloc = 0;
Q.monarchist_in_bloc = 0;
Q.falange_in_bloc = 0;
Q.other_in_bloc = 0;

// CNT-FAI did not officially endorse the Popular Front, but rank-and-file
// participation was far higher than in 1933.
Q.anarchist_electoral_stance = 1;
Q.anarchist_strength = 35;

Q.industrial_psoe = 42;
Q.industrial_pce = 14;
Q.industrial_ceda = 5;
Q.industrial_izq_rep = 12;
Q.industrial_radical = 6;
Q.industrial_monarchist = 2;
Q.industrial_falange = 2;
Q.industrial_other = 17;

Q.landless_psoe = 40;
Q.landless_pce = 10;
Q.landless_ceda = 8;
Q.landless_izq_rep = 10;
Q.landless_radical = 6;
Q.landless_monarchist = 6;
Q.landless_falange = 1;
Q.landless_other = 19;

Q.smallholder_psoe = 10;
Q.smallholder_pce = 2;
Q.smallholder_ceda = 32;
Q.smallholder_izq_rep = 10;
Q.smallholder_radical = 10;
Q.smallholder_monarchist = 16;
Q.smallholder_falange = 2;
Q.smallholder_other = 18;

Q.urban_middle_psoe = 12;
Q.urban_middle_pce = 2;
Q.urban_middle_ceda = 12;
Q.urban_middle_izq_rep = 28;
Q.urban_middle_radical = 12;
Q.urban_middle_monarchist = 6;
Q.urban_middle_falange = 3;
Q.urban_middle_other = 25;

Q.unemployed_psoe = 34;
Q.unemployed_pce = 15;
Q.unemployed_ceda = 6;
Q.unemployed_izq_rep = 10;
Q.unemployed_radical = 5;
Q.unemployed_monarchist = 3;
Q.unemployed_falange = 2;
Q.unemployed_other = 25;

Q.catholic_psoe = 7;
Q.catholic_pce = 1;
Q.catholic_ceda = 42;
Q.catholic_izq_rep = 6;
Q.catholic_radical = 8;
Q.catholic_monarchist = 20;
Q.catholic_falange = 2;
Q.catholic_other = 14;
!}
go-to: election_algorithm
set-jump: post_election

@post_election
on-arrival: {!
// set congress proportion to votes (this harness has no adjustmentFactors/
// bloc-bonus post-processing of its own -- run @post_election_1928 in
// events/election_1928.scene.dry for the full seat-allocation pipeline)
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    Q[party + '_r'] = Q[party + '_votes'];
}

Q.largest_party = 'PSOE';
if (Q.ceda_r >= Q.psoe_r && Q.ceda_r >= Q.pce_r) {
    Q.largest_party = 'CEDA';
}
if (Q.pce_r >= Q.psoe_r && Q.pce_r >= Q.ceda_r) {
    Q.largest_party = 'PCE';
}

// Spanish coalition possibilities (a small, curated set -- see
// docs/planning/BC_election_engine_execution_plan.md, C-5)
Q.republican_socialist = Q.psoe_r + Q.izq_rep_r + Q.radical_r;
Q.radical_ceda = Q.radical_r + Q.ceda_r;
Q.popular_front = Q.psoe_r + Q.pce_r + Q.izq_rep_r;
Q.national_bloc = Q.ceda_r + Q.monarchist_r + Q.falange_r;
Q.workers_alliance = Q.psoe_r + Q.pce_r;
!}

The electoral system combines proportional representation with the 1933 majoritarian bloc-list law: coalesced lists receive a seat bonus, solo lists a penalty (run through `events/election_1928.scene.dry`'s `@post_election_1928` for the full pipeline -- this harness only shows raw vote-to-seat before that adjustment).

**Election results (raw vote share, pre-bloc-adjustment):**

PSOE: [+ psoe_r +]

PCE: [+ pce_r +]

CEDA: [+ ceda_r +]

Republican Left (IR): [+ izq_rep_r +]

Radical Party (PRR): [+ radical_r +]

Monarchist: [+ monarchist_r +]

Falange: [+ falange_r +]

Other: [+ other_r +]

**Potential coalitions:**

Republican-Socialist (PSOE + IR + Radicals, 1931-style): [+ republican_socialist +]

Radical-CEDA Bloc (1933-style): [+ radical_ceda +]

Popular Front (PSOE + PCE + IR, 1936-style): [+ popular_front +]

National Bloc (CEDA + Monarchist + Falange): [+ national_bloc +]

Workers' Alliance (PSOE + PCE): [+ workers_alliance +]
